  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116184",
      "title": "Introducing The async Pipe",
      "lectureOrder": 205,
      "videoOrder": 197,
      "sourceHash": "df6f91b831682c141c5478b252621346fb5e96be087b2585d363c0340c77016f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.287,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "So using such a rxjs subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "and setting up that subscription here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "and triggering change detection manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "can be a good alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "to using signals when using OnPush components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 17.043,
          "en": "and services in combination.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.94,
          "end": 20.52,
          "en": "However, as you can tell, this was of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.52,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "quite a lot of code we had to write here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "in this messages-list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "And that's why Angular also offers a shortcut,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "a built-in feature, if you want to call it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "for situations like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 39.12,
          "en": "Instead of managing this messages property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.12,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "and instead of triggering change detection manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 46.08,
          "en": "and injecting this change detector reference thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.08,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "and instead of managing the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "and its cleanup, instead of doing all these things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 58.98,
          "en": "you can get rid of all that code, get rid of that interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.98,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "and get rid of all these imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 63.033,
          "en": "which are not needed anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.74,
          "end": 66.69,
          "en": "And instead of doing all these things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.69,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "you can add one simple new property to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "Let's maybe name it messages$ as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "though the name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 78.723,
          "en": "and does not have to be the same one as in the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "But here I will use the same one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "because I, in the end, wanna bind my messages subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 88.413,
          "en": "from the service to the messages here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 91.92,
          "en": "Now what will this achieve though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "Well, now this property holds a behavior subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 99.993,
          "en": "which emits events that carry that messages array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "Angular now offers us a special pipe we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "in the template to automatically set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "and clean up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 116.31,
          "en": "and read those values from the subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.31,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "For that, I'll use my messages$ property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 123.813,
          "en": "and then I'll use the special async pipe thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 126.972,
          "en": "And that's a built-in pipe that's meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.972,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "to be used in conjunction with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "which is the main thing this rxjs package offers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 137.1,
          "en": "And in the end, that subject we're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.1,
          "end": 141.78,
          "en": "that behavior subject, is also just kind of an observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "and we'll dive a bit deeper into rxjs later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 147.993,
          "en": "For now, that's all you need to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 150.9,
          "en": "So async is a built-in pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 153.63,
          "en": "that can be used on such an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 156.39,
          "en": "on such a subject here, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "and behind the scenes when using this async pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 164.19,
          "en": "Angular will set up a subscription, will read the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.19,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "that are emitted by that subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.62,
          "en": "and will provide them here in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.62,
          "end": 172.797,
          "en": "so that this for loop will continue to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.797,
          "end": 176.462,
          "en": "And it will also unsubscribe if this component shouldn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.462,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "be active anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.86,
          "end": 183.3,
          "en": "In addition, it will also trigger change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "for this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "whenever a new value is received from that subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 190.62,
          "en": "or from that observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "So that's also something the async pipe will do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "It will trigger change detection when new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 198.123,
          "en": "are received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.68,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "Now I just have to enable it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 205.62,
          "en": "by adding the imports array in that messages-list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.62,
          "end": 208.683,
          "en": "and by adding the async pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.7,
          "end": 212.793,
          "en": "and for that you must import it from Angular common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.35,
          "end": 217.11,
          "en": "With it imported and unlocked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "this will work though, and as a result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "the application will work the same way it did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 226.82999999999998,
          "en": "So here, if I enter test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 229.623,
          "en": "and I save this, you see that shows up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 235.38,
          "en": "If I add testing, clean this and click save,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.38,
          "end": 238.41,
          "en": "you see the messages-list component was evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 241.65,
          "en": "because the async pipe triggered the change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 243.423,
          "en": "and the message shows up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "and that's therefore a more elegant way of handling this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 250.2,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it's super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.2,
          "end": 252.96,
          "en": "to understand what's going on behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.96,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "And if you ever need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 258.24,
          "en": "to do more than just output the subject value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.24,
          "end": 262.23,
          "en": "in your template, you will need to manually set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 266.04,
          "en": "and manage such a subscription as I showed it to you before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.04,
          "end": 269.94,
          "en": "That's why you should know about both approaches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 271.053,
          "en": "and now you do.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
